# Publish target is the public registry. `publishConfig.registry` in package.json
# pins it, so `npm publish` still works when the user-level ~/.npmrc points at a
# read-only mirror (registry.npmmirror.com) — that is the default on this machine.
#
# The package is unscoped since 1.7.0 (`dsh-native`), so no scope mapping is needed
# here. The old `@keer1024` -> npm.pkg.github.com mapping is gone together with the
# GitHub Packages channel; the legacy scoped 1.6.1 on npmjs stays installable.
#
# The token is never committed: export NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, or let actions/setup-node
# write it from the NPM_TOKEN secret in .github/workflows/publish.yml (repo root).
# //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
